{"qid":"Q750","names":["Bolivia"],"title":"Bolivia","endonym":{"native":"Wuliwya Suyu","lang":"ay"},"capsule":"Bolivia was declared an independent republic on 6 August 1825, carved from the Spanish Viceroyalty of Peru and named after Simón Bolívar; the dataset records it from 1825 to 2024. The country lost its Pacific coastal littoral to Chile in the War of the Pacific (1879–1884) and the Chaco Boreal to Paraguay after the Chaco War (1932–1935), leaving Bolivia landlocked. The 1952 National Revolution under the MNR (Movimiento Nacionalista Revolucionario) nationalized the tin mines and introduced universal suffrage, marking the most significant social transformation in the republic's history. Bolivia experienced repeated military coups between the 1960s and 1982, when civilian democracy was restored; Evo Morales served as the country's first indigenous president from 2006 to 2019.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Bolivia's borders are defined by modern treaty law and are well-documented, though the Chaco frontier was formally settled only by the 1938 peace treaty with Paraguay; internal administrative boundaries are precisely mapped.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Bolivia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Bolivia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Bolivia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolivia"}],"britannica":"place/Bolivia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Bolivia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q8605","name":"Simón Bolívar","start":1825,"end":1825,"image":"Simón Bolívar by Acevedo Bernal, 1922.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sim%C3%B3n%20Bol%C3%ADvar%20by%20Acevedo%20Bernal%2C%201922.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Ricardo Acevedo Bernal","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Simuna Wuliwar","nativeLang":"ay"},{"qid":"Q189779","name":"Antonio José de Sucre","start":1825,"end":1828,"image":"Martin Tovar y Tovar 12.JPG","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Martin%20Tovar%20y%20Tovar%2012.JPG?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Martín Tovar y Tovar (1827 - 1902)","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q286657","name":"Pedro Blanco Soto","start":1828,"end":1829,"image":"Pedro Blanco Soto.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pedro%20Blanco%20Soto.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"The original uploader was Villalad at English Wikipedia.","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Pedro Blanco","nativeLang":"ay"},{"qid":"Q734654","name":"José María Pérez de Urdininea","start":1828,"end":1828,"image":"Jose maria perez de urdinena.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jose%20maria%20perez%20de%20urdinena.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"José María Pérez","nativeLang":"ay"},{"qid":"Q5945023","name":"José Ramón de Loayza Pacheco","start":1828,"end":1828,"image":"Loazya.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Loazya.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Vicepresidencia del Estado Plurinacional de Bolivia","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q467959","name":"Andrés de Santa Cruz","start":1829,"end":1839,"image":"Andrés de Santa Cruz. Ugalde, Manuel. c. 1835, Andrés de Santa Cruz collection, La Paz.png","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Andr%C3%A9s%20de%20Santa%20Cruz.%20Ugalde%2C%20Manuel.%20c.%201835%2C%20Andr%C3%A9s%20de%20Santa%20Cruz%20collection%2C%20La%